; setline_spin_sample_out_of_domain: spin is {-1, +1}, which is not a range.
;
; This is the vector a bounds-only domain check fails. Spin's envelope is
; [-1, 1] and 0 sits inside it, so `low <= v <= high` admits a value that is
; not a spin at all -- an assignment no Ising solver can read. Domain::contains
; is therefore defined per domain rather than derived from Domain::bounds,
; and Domain::step exists to say the thing the envelope cannot: spin strides
; by 2.
;
; 0 is also the default for the other two domains, which makes it exactly the
; value a guard written once and reused everywhere would let through.

PUSH 4
SSMX r0          ; spin sample, domain {-1, +1}, defaults to -1

PUSH 1
PUSH 0           ; inside the envelope, outside the domain
SETLINE r0
HALT
